# Showcase component page structure

Use **`ShowcaseDocPage`** + **`ShowcaseDocSection`** (`section` = canonical id from `showcaseDoc.ts`).  
Do **not** use raw `ShowcasePageLayout` for new component docs.

Import primitives from `../primitives`. Tokens: follow `prytula-design-system.mdc`.

---

## Page chrome (always)

| # | Block | Implementation |
|---|--------|----------------|
| 1 | **Page header** | `ShowcaseDocPage` — `title` (H1), `description` (one line), optional `status`, `updatedAt`, `version` |
| 14 | **Page footer** | `ShowcaseDocPage` — `figmaUrl` (CS node), optional `feedbackHref` |

`showViewportBar={true}` only when preview width matters (rare for simple components).

---

## Live preview viewport switch (default for component pages)

When the user asks for **«переключалось по розмірам»** (or the component is responsive / section-scale), wire **`ShowcaseDocLivePreview`** with the **five named breakpoints**:

| Toggle label   | Frame width |
|----------------|-------------|
| Wide desktop   | 1920px      |
| Desktop        | 1440px      |
| Laptop         | 1200px      |
| Tablet         | 768px       |
| Mobile         | 375px       |

**Implementation** (see `PartnersShowcase.tsx`, `ProjectCardShowcase.tsx`, `PartnerCardShowcase.tsx`):

```tsx
const [previewViewportId, setPreviewViewportId] =
  useState<ShowcaseViewportId>("1440");
const previewWidth = showcaseViewportWidth(previewViewportId);

<ShowcaseDocLivePreview
  caption={`${showcaseViewportName(previewViewportId)} (${previewWidth}px) · …`}
  previewViewport
  previewViewportId={previewViewportId}
  onPreviewViewportChange={setPreviewViewportId}
  flush
>
  …
</ShowcaseDocLivePreview>
```

- Import `ShowcaseViewportId`, `showcaseViewportName`, `showcaseViewportWidth` from `../primitives`.
- If the component has Figma **Size** (`desktop` | `tablet` | `mobile`), also pass `size={figmaComponentSizeForViewportWidth(previewWidth)}`.
- Do **not** nest extra `ShowcasePreview` inside `ShowcaseDocLivePreview` — the live preview primitive already wraps the frame.
- Smaller components (Link Card, …) may use `previewSizeOptions` (Desktop / Tablet / Mobile) **in addition** when Figma Size matters; section-scale pages use viewport switch only.

---

## Body sections (top → bottom)

| # | Section id | Title (default) | Primitives / notes |
|---|------------|-----------------|---------------------|
| 2 | `live-preview` | Live preview | `ShowcaseDocLivePreview` — neutral `ShowcasePreview`, hero variant, **caption**, optional `code` + Copy code |
| 3 | `variants-gallery` | Variants gallery | `ShowcaseMatrix` and/or grid of instances; **full variant name** in caption; group by Figma property (rows/cols) |
| 4 | `anatomy` | Anatomy | `ShowcaseDocAnatomy` — diagram + labeled parts (full genre only) |
| 5 | `properties` | Properties | `ShowcaseDocPropertiesTable` — Property \| Type \| Options/default \| Description; `typeKind`: VARIANT / TEXT / BOOLEAN / INSTANCE_SWAP |
| 6 | `token-usage` | Token usage | `ShowcaseDocTokenUsageTable` — Element \| Property \| Token \| Value (resolved) |
| 7 | `states-interactions` | States & interactions | Separate row per state if not covered in gallery (full genre) |
| 8 | `sizes` | Sizes | Side-by-side S/M/L or breakpoints (full genre, if applicable) |
| 9 | `accessibility` | Accessibility | `ShowcaseDocBulletList` — keyboard, ARIA, hit target, focus, SR |
| 10 | `usage-guidelines` | Usage guidelines | `ShowcaseDocUsageGuidelines` — do / don't / **alternatives** (links) |
| 11 | `examples` | Examples / recipes | Product context blocks + code (full genre) |
| 12 | `related-components` | Related components | `ShowcaseDocRelated` — siblings + «used with» |
| 13 | `changelog` | Changelog | `ShowcaseDocChangelog` — optional |

---

## Genre checklists (`showcaseDoc.ts`)

**Minimal** (Checkbox, Radiobutton, Badge, …): sections **2, 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 12**  
→ `SHOWCASE_DOC_MINIMAL_SECTIONS`

**Full** (Donation Widget, Menu, TextField, …): sections **2–12**, optional **13**  
→ `SHOWCASE_DOC_FULL_SECTIONS`

Helper: `getShowcaseDocSections("component-minimal" | "component-full")`.

---

## Section order

Render sections in the **same order** as the checklist. Do not reorder (e.g. props before gallery on minimal pages).

Foundations (Colors, Spacing, …): **no** live preview; start at `variants-gallery`; see `SHOWCASE_DOC_FOUNDATION_SECTIONS`.

